---
source: compiler-core/src/javascript/tests/module_lets.rs
expression: "\npub let a = b\n\npub let b = a\n"
---
----- SOURCE CODE

pub let a = b

pub let b = a


----- ERROR
error: Value used before it is defined
  ┌─ /src/one/two.gleam:2:1
  │
2 │ pub let a = b
  │ ^^^^^^^^^ This reads `b`
3 │ 
4 │ pub let b = a
  │ --------- Defined here

`b` is bound below this one, and a binding at module level
runs when the module is loaded, in the order it was written. So
`b` has no value yet when this one runs.
